questions.solution:
Ethanol gives trichloromethane on distilling with bleaching powder.
$\begin{aligned}
&\text{ (I) } \mathrm{Cl}_{2}+\mathrm{H}_{2} \mathrm{O} \longrightarrow 2 \mathrm{HCl}+[\mathrm{O}] \\
&\mathrm{CH}_{3} \mathrm{CH}_{2} \mathrm{OH}+[\mathrm{O}] \longrightarrow \mathrm{CH}_{3} \mathrm{CHO}+\mathrm{H}_{2} \mathrm{O}
\end{aligned}$
Ethanol
(II) $\mathrm{CH}_{3} \mathrm{CHO}+3 \mathrm{Cl}_{2} \longrightarrow \mathrm{CCl}_{3} \mathrm{CHO}+3 \mathrm{HCl}
(III) \mathrm{CCl}_{3} \mathrm{CHO}+\mathrm{Ca}(\mathrm{OH})_{2} \longrightarrow 2 \mathrm{CHCl}_{3}+(\mathrm{HCOO})_{2} \mathrm{Ca}
Trichloro methane$

